{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43936-street-fighter-rpg","id":43936,"title":"Street Fighter RPG","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-06T20:56:15-08:00","id":43936,"title":"Street Fighter RPG","content":"Does anyone still play this one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T21:25:40-08:00","id":43950,"title":"","content":"Still play, well not so much but the game is ongoing and eventually might get piked up again. Me and my group treated it pretty seriously which led to it being one of the stranger, dramatic games we've played over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Things need not have happened to be true. Tales and dreams are the shadow truths that will endure when mere facts are dust and ashes, and forgot.&quot; Sandman (Neil Gaiman)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/733-troller","name":"Troller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T00:22:10-08:00","id":44003,"title":"","content":"Did you have to tweak it? If so, in what way? Also, did you add to the setting or just use the various storyline expansions in the Street Fighter video games? I was thinking to maybe use the rules but for Mortal Kombat setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T06:48:48-08:00","id":44136,"title":"","content":"It has been a while since I last played it, but it is in the repertoire for my group. In fact, it is one of the few games that other players in my group also ST sometimes (usually I'm forever the ST/DM/GM/HG/whatever)<br /> <br /> We do use a lot of house-rules and homebrew material. Also, most of us are SNK fans, so the games tend to happen in that universe, usually having to do with the King of Fighters tournament. The Street Fighter setting was used only once by us, I think.<br /> <br /> Also used it for a really short lived game set in the Rurouni Kenshin (aka Samurai X) universe, as well as a couple homebrew settings","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:15:34-08:00","id":44146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43936-street-fighter-rpg?p=44003#post44003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you have to tweak it? If so, in what way? Also, did you add to the setting or just use the various storyline expansions in the Street Fighter video games? I was thinking to maybe use the rules but for Mortal Kombat setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all you want is mechanics, I recommend picking up a copy of <b>Shards of the Exalted Dream</b> and using the rules from &quot;Burn Legend.&quot; They are heavily inspired by <b>Street Fighter</b>'s rules, but are much simpler and faster paced. &quot;Burn Legend&quot; also has way better supernatural powers and a wider variety of character options. You might also like the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:08:27-08:00","id":44216,"title":"","content":"I personally don't play it, but I know people who do. Yet that same group keeps trying to find a better system to replace it with. They have yet to find one that gets a simple majority vote in favor of it at their table, so they keep playing Street Fighter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:55:49-08:00","id":44253,"title":"","content":"@JimB...I have all the books. I also did not enjoy the Burn Legend Shard. <br /> @Dairugger..I know the feeling. It is why our group usually defaults to White Wolf/Onyx Path games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:05:53-08:00","id":44297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43936-street-fighter-rpg?p=44146#post44146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Burn Legend&quot; also has way better supernatural powers and a wider variety of character options. You might also like the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't checked it out as well, but &quot;Burn Legend&quot; sounds like it might work for a Guilty Gear RPG. A fighting game set in a post-apocalyptic fantasy setting that has tons of back story and atmosphere behind it. It's still one I'm surprised no one has made a fan supplement of with basic rules or Exalted rules.<br /> <br /> <b>@ thedonnie:</b> One of the vaporware books set for the Street Fighter RPG was a Dark Stalkers book. Once the deal between Capcom and White Wolf ended, White Wolf couldn't print a few books they were going to put out for it. That also resulted in World of Darkness: Combat being put out.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:17:51-08:00","id":44306,"title":"","content":"Burn Legend is an interesting world, but I GM'd a game for it once and it was not a good time. My players don't really like PvP and the fighting took too goddamn long.<br /> <br /> Though the latter probably happened because I misread the rules about Health Stocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:46:04-08:00","id":44538,"title":"","content":"I think I have the Street Fighter book as a pdf. Wait, let me check.<br /> <br /> Yep, sure did. Dunno where I got it but it can't have been legal. Probably when I copied some friend's old CD-ROMs. I don't think I've ever read it, and looking at it now, I'm not sure I will. Between school, Exalted 3e and all other media that you want to get into these days, I've just no time.<br /> <br /> I've always wanted to play more Burn Legend, and I think it's one of the better systems for playing online as well. What little I've played of it suggests that while the basic combat system (which I define as the idea of rolling dice pools against each other, not against a defense, and each move cancelling a certain move type outright) is freaking brilliant, the extra bits they put on can use some polish. Actually, make that a whole lot of polish. I also find that combats go on a bit too long, and while it's easy to just reduce health pools, it also affects stuff like Overdrive and Ultimates. Further, I think the original batch of Techniques are pretty scattered and not as thorough as they could be. I really wish it'd get more development, because it's almost criminal to leave such a promising basic system hanging like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T18:34:58-08:00","id":44596,"title":"","content":"Trivia regarding the Brazilian version of the SF RPG: you know all those awful illustrations in the game, including the cover? Yeah, the translated version got those removed, with much better, classic official capcom artwork in their place. Too bad only the basic stuff was ever translated - makes me wonder if they would find a solution for the incredibly bad character pictures in some of the later books in the line. On the other hand those are so bad they are at least funny, so maybe it is best to leave that as is XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T19:39:12-08:00","id":44617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43936-street-fighter-rpg?p=44297#post44297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the vaporware books set for the Street Fighter RPG was a Dark Stalkers book. Once the deal between Capcom and White Wolf ended, White Wolf couldn't print a few books they were going to put out for it. That also resulted in World of Darkness: Combat being put out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one would have <i>bought the hell</i> out of a <b>Darkstalkers</b> book, whether or not it prevented the Big Book of Beating Ass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:52:18-08:00","id":44643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AberrantEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43936-street-fighter-rpg?p=44617#post44617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I for one would have <i>bought the hell</i> out of a <b>Darkstalkers</b> book, whether or not it prevented the Big Book of Beating Ass.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KiHRLUIZzs4\" target=\"_blank\">Just as long as the USA Animation series was kept as far away as possible.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}